WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:15.282
Hi! When you meet a word you don't know, don't panic. The sentence often hides clues that help you work out the meaning. Today we'll learn how to answer vocabulary questions, and look at synonyms and antonyms.

2
00:00:15.432 --> 00:00:22.578
Look at this: after the long hike, Dad was exhausted. After walking so far, how would he feel?

3
00:00:22.728 --> 00:00:27.690
So exhausted means very tired. The clue is the long hike.

4
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:36.930
In a multiple-choice question, put each option back into the sentence and read it. Choose the one that makes the best sense.

5
00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:45.714
Synonyms have almost the same meaning. Huge and enormous both mean very big. Begin and start both mean the same thing.

6
00:00:45.864 --> 00:00:55.794
Antonyms have opposite meanings. Generous means happy to share, and selfish is the opposite. Ancient means very old, and modern means new.

7
00:00:55.944 --> 00:01:04.482
The same word can mean different things. A bright light is a shining light, but a bright pupil is a clever pupil.

8
00:01:04.632 --> 00:01:10.698
In a vocabulary cloze, read the whole passage first, so you know what the story is about.

9
00:01:10.848 --> 00:01:19.986
Then ask what kind of word the ___ needs: a noun, a verb or an adjective? Finally, check that the meaning makes sense.

10
00:01:20.136 --> 00:01:26.394
Watch out! Many pupils choose an answer by looking at the word alone, and get it wrong!

11
00:01:26.544 --> 00:01:30.906
A word like bright means different things in different sentences.

12
00:01:31.056 --> 00:01:37.314
Always put the option back into the sentence and check which one fits best.

13
00:01:37.464 --> 00:01:48.306
Your turn! The timid kitten hid under the bed when visitors came. What does timid mean? Pause and think.

14
00:01:48.456 --> 00:01:57.162
Timid means shy and easily frightened. The clue is that it hid when visitors came. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:57.312 --> 00:02:08.586
Another one! Mrs Tan was furious when the boys broke her window. What does furious mean? Pause and think.

16
00:02:08.736 --> 00:02:17.610
Furious means very angry. Her window was broken, so of course she was angry. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:28.434
One more! The ancient temple was built hundreds of years ago. What does ancient mean? Pause and think.

18
00:02:28.584 --> 00:02:36.138
Ancient means very old. The clue is hundreds of years ago. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:36.288 --> 00:02:44.394
Next one! What is the opposite of generous? Pause and think.

20
00:02:44.544 --> 00:02:53.514
Selfish. A generous person is happy to share, and a selfish person is not. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:53.664 --> 00:03:02.346
Last one! Which word has the same meaning as huge? Pause and think.

22
00:03:02.496 --> 00:03:07.722
Enormous, or very big. Did you get it right?

23
00:03:07.872 --> 00:03:14.802
Remember: for a word you don't know, look for clues in the sentence, then put each option back in and read it.

24
00:03:14.952 --> 00:03:22.722
Synonyms mean the same, and antonyms mean the opposite. The same word can mean different things in different sentences.

25
00:03:22.872 --> 00:03:27.978
When you read today, find a new word and guess its meaning!

